1
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:52,077
I'm a reindeer!

2
00:01:52,077 --> 00:01:53,077
It just talks!

3
00:01:56,077 --> 00:01:59,077
Pirate this, pirate that, who cares?

4
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,077
I hate pirates!

5
00:02:00,077 --> 00:02:02,077
Every stinking last one of them!

6
00:02:02,077 --> 00:02:04,077
So why would I be on this ship?

7
00:02:04,077 --> 00:02:06,077
The only things I love are money and tangerines,

8
00:02:06,077 --> 00:02:08,077
and I don't see either around here.

9
00:02:10,077 --> 00:02:12,077
It's a little early for this much of a racket.

10
00:02:12,077 --> 00:02:14,077
I was trying to sleep.

11
00:02:14,077 --> 00:02:17,077
There's gotta be some way off this ship.

12
00:02:21,077 --> 00:02:25,077
I don't know what's going on here,

13
00:02:25,077 --> 00:02:28,077
but I don't see any point in sticking around.

14
00:02:30,077 --> 00:02:34,077
A mysterious boy with a horn and Robin's deduction!

15
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,077
Our navigator.

16
00:02:45,077 --> 00:02:47,077
I guess I can postpone that heart attack.

17
00:02:47,077 --> 00:02:49,077
Not that I'm sad to see that guy go,

18
00:02:49,077 --> 00:02:51,077
but we're losing people left and right.

19
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:53,077
Our navigator's likely headed for the island.

20
00:02:53,077 --> 00:02:55,077
I doubt she'll go too far.

21
00:02:55,077 --> 00:02:57,077
She won't do anything drastic.

22
00:02:57,077 --> 00:02:59,077
Not until she thinks things through anyway.

23
00:02:59,077 --> 00:03:00,077
Let's hope so.

24
00:03:04,077 --> 00:03:06,077
I'm starving to death here!

25
00:03:07,077 --> 00:03:08,077
You look delicious!

26
00:03:09,077 --> 00:03:10,077
Jeez.

27
00:03:10,077 --> 00:03:13,077
You've really got a one-track mind, don't you?

28
00:03:13,077 --> 00:03:14,077
Mm.

29
00:03:15,077 --> 00:03:16,077
Oh well.

30
00:03:16,077 --> 00:03:17,077
I guess we can try to figure out

31
00:03:17,077 --> 00:03:20,077
just what the hell is going on here while we're eating.

32
00:03:20,077 --> 00:03:21,077
But first things first,

33
00:03:21,077 --> 00:03:23,077
I'm afraid I never caught your name, miss.

34
00:03:24,077 --> 00:03:25,077
It's Nico Robin.

35
00:03:26,077 --> 00:03:28,077
Despite the circumstances, it's a pleasure.

36
00:03:28,077 --> 00:03:30,077
Can you fill us in on our history?

37
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:32,077
Sure.

38
00:03:32,077 --> 00:03:33,077
There's no way in hell.

39
00:03:33,077 --> 00:03:34,077
I wouldn't be caught dead on that ship.

40
00:03:34,077 --> 00:03:35,077
The only thing pirates are good for

41
00:03:35,077 --> 00:03:36,077
is destroying other people's lives.

42
00:03:36,077 --> 00:03:37,077
I've got to figure out some way

43
00:03:37,077 --> 00:03:38,077
to get back to Kokoyashi Village.

44
00:03:38,077 --> 00:03:39,077
Come on ashore, lady.

45
00:03:39,077 --> 00:03:40,077
I'm glad that you've wandered my way.

46
00:03:40,077 --> 00:03:41,077
Very glad indeed.

47
00:03:42,077 --> 00:03:43,077
We have to find theükle,

48
00:03:43,077 --> 00:03:44,077
but you have to go.

49
00:03:44,077 --> 00:03:45,077
There's no way in hell.

50
00:03:45,077 --> 00:03:47,077
I wouldn't be caught dead on that ship.

51
00:03:47,077 --> 00:03:48,077
The only thing pirates are good for

52
00:03:48,077 --> 00:03:50,077
is destroying other people's lives.

53
00:03:50,077 --> 00:03:51,077
I've got to figure out some way

54
00:03:51,077 --> 00:03:52,077
to get back to Kokoyashi Village.

55
00:03:53,077 --> 00:03:54,077
Uh-uh...

56
00:04:00,077 --> 00:04:02,077
Come on ashore, lady.

57
00:04:02,077 --> 00:04:04,957
I'm glad that you've wandered my way.

58
00:04:05,397 --> 00:04:06,977
Very glad indeed.

59
00:04:15,497 --> 00:04:17,777
I haven't seen a single person.

60
00:04:18,697 --> 00:04:19,997
It's a little creepy.

61
00:04:23,057 --> 00:04:26,017
Maybe I'll find someone a little further up the hill.

62
00:04:32,077 --> 00:04:41,877
A news booth?

63
00:04:45,817 --> 00:04:46,597
What the?

64
00:04:49,657 --> 00:04:51,357
What do you people want?

65
00:04:57,357 --> 00:04:58,637
It's fine, dammit!

66
00:04:58,697 --> 00:05:00,657
Shut up! It's the only thing I can rely on!

67
00:05:00,657 --> 00:05:02,057
Well, too bad for you, then!

68
00:05:02,537 --> 00:05:03,657
Let go, jerk!

69
00:05:04,237 --> 00:05:05,877
I need it more than you do!

70
00:05:06,057 --> 00:05:07,437
Shut up! It's mine!

71
00:05:07,477 --> 00:05:09,257
I had it first! Now drop it!

72
00:05:09,317 --> 00:05:10,457
Do I look like I care?

73
00:05:10,497 --> 00:05:11,917
Who do you think you are?

74
00:05:11,997 --> 00:05:13,977
If I knew that, there wouldn't be a problem!

75
00:05:14,117 --> 00:05:15,657
What is wrong with these people?

76
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:25,297
What was that about?

77
00:05:25,697 --> 00:05:26,017
Hey.

78
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:31,737
You look perplexed.

79
00:05:31,857 --> 00:05:32,677
What's the matter?

80
00:05:35,557 --> 00:05:35,997
Hmm.

81
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:38,037
So that's it? You need a boat?

82
00:05:38,237 --> 00:05:38,597
Yeah.

83
00:05:39,137 --> 00:05:41,677
The boats docked behind us are the only ones on the island.

84
00:05:42,237 --> 00:05:43,537
What? Are you sure?

85
00:05:43,817 --> 00:05:46,737
They all look pretty run-down like no one's used them in forever.

86
00:05:46,737 --> 00:05:51,677
I guess everyone around here is too busy with other things to bother with them.

87
00:05:52,397 --> 00:05:55,177
You can go ahead and check the rest of the island if you don't believe me.

88
00:05:55,677 --> 00:05:58,477
It's a small island. It won't take you long at all.

89
00:05:59,857 --> 00:06:04,217
You ought to stick around for a while. Might as well take it easy and enjoy yourself.

90
00:06:04,217 --> 00:06:07,717
Well, I'd like to, but I really need to get going.

91
00:06:07,877 --> 00:06:09,457
Oh. That's too bad.

92
00:06:09,777 --> 00:06:10,397
I'm sorry.

93
00:06:10,777 --> 00:06:12,537
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

94
00:06:13,277 --> 00:06:13,817
Ugh.

95
00:06:14,637 --> 00:06:17,777
Well, I'm feeling kind of worn out. I'd better head on home.

96
00:06:18,477 --> 00:06:20,077
Hang on!

97
00:06:20,457 --> 00:06:21,577
Bye! See ya!

98
00:06:21,577 --> 00:06:34,277
I can't believe I'm stuck on a boat with real pirates.

99
00:06:34,837 --> 00:06:37,197
So clouds are really as fluffy as they look?

100
00:06:37,957 --> 00:06:43,737
Ducks and dog, horsey bird. Darn it. I want to remember all this stuff.

101
00:06:44,277 --> 00:06:49,277
A Davyback fight in a marine fortress, sky islands and sand countries.

102
00:06:49,277 --> 00:06:53,217
Talk about a fantastic adventure. And this is true?

103
00:06:53,597 --> 00:06:54,757
Yes. All true.

104
00:06:55,477 --> 00:06:55,817
Huh.

105
00:06:56,517 --> 00:07:00,517
I'm sitting next to a pirate with a hundred million berry bounty on his head.

106
00:07:01,377 --> 00:07:05,037
Hey, don't you got any more stories about our neat adventures?

107
00:07:05,457 --> 00:07:11,297
I didn't join your crew until after you left Alabasta. Sorry. I couldn't tell you what happened before that.

108
00:07:11,417 --> 00:07:13,197
Oh, man. That sucks.

109
00:07:13,197 --> 00:07:20,977
I can't really say I'd buy every aspect of her story, but she's got one piece of evidence on her side.

110
00:07:21,277 --> 00:07:23,797
This is exactly how I would have set this kitchen up.

111
00:07:24,317 --> 00:07:28,457
So, Robin, can you tell us about yesterday before any of this happened?

112
00:07:28,637 --> 00:07:31,277
Sure. But let's include the ship's doctor.

113
00:07:31,537 --> 00:07:31,777
Huh?

114
00:07:31,777 --> 00:07:37,637
You're still doing it backwards.

115
00:07:39,037 --> 00:07:40,837
Shut up. I'll do it how I want.

116
00:07:40,957 --> 00:07:43,357
You've got to be hungry. Why don't you sit down and eat?

117
00:07:43,997 --> 00:07:48,277
Oh, come on. Do I look stupid to you? You really think I'm going to fall for something like that?

118
00:07:48,337 --> 00:07:53,657
This conversation is nothing without your voice. Please join us. We need your brilliant input.

119
00:07:54,657 --> 00:07:58,577
You dummy. You're not going to win me over by flattering me, okay?

120
00:07:58,697 --> 00:07:59,717
You sure about that?

121
00:07:59,717 --> 00:08:03,857
Yes. We followed the coordinates to this area of the sea.

122
00:08:05,957 --> 00:08:08,557
Nami, are you sure we haven't peered off course?

123
00:08:08,677 --> 00:08:11,057
Calm down. The log pose is never wrong.

124
00:08:11,497 --> 00:08:13,977
Hey, Usopp, what's the lookout like up there?

125
00:08:14,097 --> 00:08:15,557
Ah, give me a second.

126
00:08:17,437 --> 00:08:18,357
Island ahead!

127
00:08:20,657 --> 00:08:23,537
It looks like it's completely surrounded by coral reefs.

128
00:08:23,917 --> 00:08:26,017
It's dangerous to push ahead in this light.

129
00:08:26,017 --> 00:08:29,397
Why don't we drop anchor off the coast tonight and go ashore in the morning?

130
00:08:29,397 --> 00:08:30,237
Ah!

131
00:08:31,057 --> 00:08:33,077
Don't want to listen to your navigator, huh?

132
00:08:33,537 --> 00:08:35,517
Hey, Sanji, no dinner for Luffy.

133
00:08:35,697 --> 00:08:36,037
What?

134
00:08:36,597 --> 00:08:37,997
Whatever you say, Nami!

135
00:08:38,197 --> 00:08:39,037
I'm sorry!

136
00:08:39,617 --> 00:08:41,497
And after that, everybody went to bed.

137
00:08:41,957 --> 00:08:45,017
Well, I stayed up doing research and the swordsman was on watch.

138
00:08:45,017 --> 00:08:49,677
I know it's not much, but that's it.

139
00:08:50,617 --> 00:08:52,877
Everything's the same as you remember it after that.

140
00:08:53,257 --> 00:08:53,657
Probably.

141
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:58,937
The pirate hunter was pissed we woke him up, so he must have fallen asleep at some point.

142
00:08:59,237 --> 00:09:00,297
It would seem so.

143
00:09:01,157 --> 00:09:01,877
More coffee?

144
00:09:02,697 --> 00:09:03,757
Yes, please.

145
00:09:03,757 --> 00:09:08,937
So the big question we need to answer is why you're the only one who didn't lose your memory.

146
00:09:09,437 --> 00:09:15,877
The only difference that I can think of is that I'm the only one who stayed awake, if the swordsman did in fact fall asleep, that is.

147
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:19,997
Ah, well, I fell asleep, but I still remember that we are the Usopp pirates!

148
00:09:20,377 --> 00:09:20,977
Good point.

149
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:24,157
Sounds like it all boils down to whether we were asleep or not.

150
00:09:24,517 --> 00:09:26,337
I'm just pointing out the obvious factors.

151
00:09:26,917 --> 00:09:27,997
It could be a coincidence.

152
00:09:28,397 --> 00:09:29,917
I've never heard of such a case.

153
00:09:30,217 --> 00:09:31,417
I don't know what to think.

154
00:09:31,857 --> 00:09:34,657
Well, now that I've told you what happened, let's hear your story.

155
00:09:34,977 --> 00:09:37,317
Why don't you tell us what you think happened to you yesterday?

156
00:09:38,377 --> 00:09:45,257
I'm pretty sure that I went to pick medicinal herbs with Dr. Reen, and then I went back to the castle and went to bed and woke up here.

157
00:09:45,717 --> 00:09:47,217
Well, I'm being ignored.

158
00:09:47,217 --> 00:09:52,717
I blacked out after getting swallowed up by a giant whirlpool, and then I was here.

159
00:09:53,637 --> 00:09:54,877
Same as these guys.

160
00:09:55,097 --> 00:09:58,557
I remember going to sleep in my room after work, but then I woke up here.

161
00:09:58,897 --> 00:10:01,157
And none of you remember anything after that.

162
00:10:05,857 --> 00:10:06,737
That's right!

163
00:10:06,917 --> 00:10:07,857
There was a horn!

164
00:10:08,017 --> 00:10:10,257
I remember hearing someone blow on a horn!

165
00:10:10,357 --> 00:10:11,057
Same here!

166
00:10:11,297 --> 00:10:12,217
Yeah, horn!

167
00:10:12,357 --> 00:10:13,577
I heard the same thing!

168
00:10:13,837 --> 00:10:14,817
Yeah, me too.

169
00:10:14,817 --> 00:10:18,177
And then, a little boy suddenly appeared out of nowhere.

170
00:10:22,117 --> 00:10:22,897
Hang on.

171
00:10:23,177 --> 00:10:24,697
I don't think we lost our memories.

172
00:10:24,997 --> 00:10:27,697
I get the feeling that kids somehow stole them from us.

173
00:10:27,857 --> 00:10:29,437
Well, we don't know that just yet.

174
00:10:29,817 --> 00:10:32,997
But I'm willing to bet that this child is the answer to our situation.

175
00:10:32,997 --> 00:10:37,557
Do you think it's possible we'll lose more memories each time we fall asleep?

176
00:10:38,917 --> 00:10:40,417
Don't scare me like that!

177
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:42,897
Look, I mean, this was just a dream, right?

178
00:10:43,117 --> 00:10:45,477
That supernatural kind of mumbo-jumbo isn't real!

179
00:10:45,557 --> 00:10:47,757
You don't think it's weird we all had the same dream?

180
00:10:48,697 --> 00:10:50,237
Supernatural or not, it happened.

181
00:10:50,537 --> 00:10:53,257
Look, I don't mean to scare you, but if this keeps happening,

182
00:10:53,257 --> 00:10:56,977
it could eventually reach a point where you're incapable of remembering who you are.

183
00:10:59,857 --> 00:11:00,977
Nope, still scared!

184
00:11:01,217 --> 00:11:04,717
Say, why is it such a big deal if we remember those things or not?

185
00:11:04,797 --> 00:11:04,997
Huh?

186
00:11:05,637 --> 00:11:09,317
You know, sure, it sucks that I don't have all those fun memories anymore,

187
00:11:09,857 --> 00:11:13,537
but it's a pretty good reason for us to start over and go on new fun adventures!

188
00:11:13,817 --> 00:11:14,037
What?

189
00:11:14,137 --> 00:11:14,957
Are you crazy?

190
00:11:15,277 --> 00:11:17,817
There's a serious chance that we could lose all of our memories!

191
00:11:18,117 --> 00:11:20,557
You really want to lose all your thoughts and dreams and everything?

192
00:11:20,697 --> 00:11:21,877
None of that's gonna happen.

193
00:11:21,877 --> 00:11:24,057
Nothing can take away my dreams.

194
00:11:24,557 --> 00:11:26,617
And I know it's the same for you guys, too.

195
00:11:28,857 --> 00:11:31,117
This guy is freakishly optimistic.

196
00:11:32,057 --> 00:11:33,217
Same old captain.

197
00:11:33,557 --> 00:11:35,937
Doesn't even need his memories to know who he is.

198
00:11:36,297 --> 00:11:37,897
Kinda find him inspiring.

199
00:11:38,657 --> 00:11:38,957
Ah!

200
00:11:39,337 --> 00:11:40,457
My food's gone!

201
00:11:44,817 --> 00:11:47,337
Don't mess with another man's food, got it?

202
00:11:47,637 --> 00:11:48,417
I'm sorry.

203
00:11:48,957 --> 00:11:50,817
There's a good chance that he's crazy.

204
00:11:50,817 --> 00:11:53,637
So I'm the stupid one for taking him seriously.

205
00:12:03,877 --> 00:12:05,697
Alright, where the hell's the town?

206
00:12:05,697 --> 00:12:25,817
This is kind of exciting!

207
00:12:25,817 --> 00:12:29,717
What's that you're making there?

208
00:12:29,897 --> 00:12:31,937
It's a medicine for regaining memories.

209
00:12:32,317 --> 00:12:32,577
No!

210
00:12:32,777 --> 00:12:33,497
Don't interfere!

211
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:35,617
Find anything useful?

212
00:12:35,937 --> 00:12:36,397
No.

213
00:12:36,817 --> 00:12:39,357
Nothing suggests that it's anything but a normal island.

214
00:12:39,617 --> 00:12:39,937
Alright!

215
00:12:40,197 --> 00:12:41,137
Finally done!

216
00:12:42,817 --> 00:12:44,897
This is my greatest invention yet.

217
00:12:45,037 --> 00:12:46,257
Then I'm sure it's amazing.

218
00:12:46,497 --> 00:12:46,657
Yep.

219
00:12:46,917 --> 00:12:48,097
You called it, my friend.

220
00:12:48,597 --> 00:12:49,157
Behold!

221
00:12:49,157 --> 00:12:53,177
Thanks to me, it doesn't even matter if we lose our memories.

222
00:12:53,677 --> 00:12:56,257
I call them identity boards!

223
00:12:57,577 --> 00:12:58,597
Great idea.

224
00:12:58,997 --> 00:13:00,037
A question mark.

225
00:13:00,137 --> 00:13:00,917
That's just rude.

226
00:13:01,117 --> 00:13:03,277
I am not an emergency food source.

227
00:13:03,437 --> 00:13:04,777
What's with the hearts on mine?

228
00:13:04,977 --> 00:13:05,197
Yep.

229
00:13:05,357 --> 00:13:07,117
Now we'll always know who we are.

230
00:13:07,397 --> 00:13:08,077
Cool, huh?

231
00:13:09,537 --> 00:13:11,717
Don't waste your time on stupid stuff.

232
00:13:11,717 --> 00:13:15,137
So, I'm missing some memories, huh?

233
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:20,557
It may appear otherwise to the blind eye, but people are quite fragile things.

234
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:25,577
Zorro.

235
00:13:29,357 --> 00:13:30,557
You're lucky, Zorro.

236
00:13:30,937 --> 00:13:32,117
Being born as a man.

237
00:13:33,037 --> 00:13:35,837
All I ever wanted was to be the world's greatest swordsman.

238
00:13:36,397 --> 00:13:41,337
When girls grow up, it's natural for us to develop into physically weaker beings than men.

239
00:13:41,337 --> 00:13:42,777
It's just so frustrating.

240
00:13:42,997 --> 00:13:45,417
If only, if I'd just been born a man.

241
00:13:45,437 --> 00:13:47,737
Don't go whining like that after you beat me!

242
00:13:48,357 --> 00:13:49,817
Because it's not fair!

243
00:13:50,077 --> 00:13:51,117
You're my goal!

244
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:51,957
Zorro.

245
00:13:52,217 --> 00:13:56,677
Boy this, girl that, or you're gonna keep up that same kind of talk after I beat you someday!

246
00:13:56,977 --> 00:13:58,097
Like skill is irrelevant!

247
00:13:58,397 --> 00:14:01,657
That's an insult to all of the training I've been pouring on every day!

248
00:14:02,337 --> 00:14:03,057
It's crap!

249
00:14:03,577 --> 00:14:04,597
Now promise me!

250
00:14:04,597 --> 00:14:08,657
Promise me that someday one of us will be the world's greatest swordsman!

251
00:14:08,657 --> 00:14:11,417
We'll compete and see who gets there!

252
00:14:13,917 --> 00:14:16,257
Dummy, you're so weak.

253
00:14:18,177 --> 00:14:19,357
It's a promise!

254
00:14:21,237 --> 00:14:25,037
Sensei, I ask that you let me have that sword.

255
00:14:25,857 --> 00:14:26,577
Her sword?

256
00:14:26,777 --> 00:14:27,377
Kawina's?

257
00:14:27,577 --> 00:14:28,277
That's right!

258
00:14:28,437 --> 00:14:30,797
I'm gonna get stronger than she ever was!

259
00:14:31,177 --> 00:14:33,497
Strong enough that my name reaches up to heaven!

260
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:36,657
I am going to be the world's greatest swordsman!

261
00:14:36,997 --> 00:14:38,037
I promised her!

262
00:14:39,037 --> 00:14:40,577
I promised!

263
00:14:40,897 --> 00:14:41,457
I did!

264
00:14:43,117 --> 00:14:43,837
Yes.

265
00:14:44,297 --> 00:14:45,677
The sword is yours.

266
00:14:52,817 --> 00:14:57,757
I leave her spirit and her dreams in your hands.

267
00:14:57,757 --> 00:15:04,337
I trained every day after that until I set out to sea in search of that man.

268
00:15:05,057 --> 00:15:06,477
And that's the last I remember.

269
00:15:07,417 --> 00:15:09,777
Falling asleep shortly after getting on a boat.

270
00:15:10,437 --> 00:15:13,297
And after that, it's like nothing else ever happened.

271
00:15:14,137 --> 00:15:16,217
And the weirdest thing about it is these swords.

272
00:15:16,777 --> 00:15:18,937
I have no idea how I got these two.

273
00:15:19,497 --> 00:15:21,457
But they feel so familiar somehow.

274
00:15:22,417 --> 00:15:23,697
None of this makes sense.

275
00:15:23,697 --> 00:15:26,677
Hey, who's back there?

276
00:15:40,957 --> 00:15:45,457
The last date recorded in the logbook is the day before the date on the newspaper.

277
00:15:45,877 --> 00:15:47,257
Which means it's current.

278
00:15:47,617 --> 00:15:48,077
But...

279
00:15:48,077 --> 00:15:56,137
How am I supposed to believe this?

280
00:15:56,577 --> 00:15:57,617
Everything she said.

281
00:15:57,997 --> 00:15:59,077
If it's true...

282
00:16:01,077 --> 00:16:02,777
That would make me a pirate.

283
00:16:03,397 --> 00:16:03,737
Me!

284
00:16:04,397 --> 00:16:05,517
I can't be!

285
00:16:05,957 --> 00:16:07,417
There's no way that it's true.

286
00:16:08,237 --> 00:16:09,077
But then...

287
00:16:09,797 --> 00:16:10,077
This tattoo...

288
00:16:11,037 --> 00:16:11,977
What happened to it?

289
00:16:13,077 --> 00:16:14,837
I don't know what's going on.

290
00:16:14,837 --> 00:16:18,077
I'm so confused.

291
00:16:20,497 --> 00:16:23,917
Greetings and salutations, you pathetic little humans!

292
00:16:24,297 --> 00:16:28,857
From this moment on, this entire island and its inhabitants are a part of my domain!

293
00:16:29,517 --> 00:16:32,677
Starting today, every one of you will pay me for your lives.

294
00:16:32,857 --> 00:16:35,477
Those who cannot pay will die!

295
00:16:36,337 --> 00:16:36,837
No.

296
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:38,597
I don't want to...

297
00:16:38,597 --> 00:16:40,177
Why do we have to leave?

298
00:16:40,177 --> 00:16:40,477
I...

299
00:16:40,477 --> 00:16:41,197
I...

300
00:16:41,197 --> 00:16:43,337
I want to stay in this village!

301
00:16:44,097 --> 00:16:48,077
It's because we're poor and that's why we can't stay together!

302
00:16:50,137 --> 00:16:50,997
Hold it!

303
00:16:51,657 --> 00:16:51,977
Hmm?

304
00:16:52,517 --> 00:16:54,997
That money I gave up was for my two daughters.

305
00:16:55,637 --> 00:16:57,457
But I can't pay you.

306
00:16:58,597 --> 00:16:59,117
Bidimi!

307
00:16:59,377 --> 00:17:00,157
You can't!

308
00:17:00,157 --> 00:17:01,617
No, it'll be okay.

309
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:02,237
Really.

310
00:17:02,797 --> 00:17:05,077
I have to do this for my family.

311
00:17:05,617 --> 00:17:07,577
Even if it costs me my life.

312
00:17:08,717 --> 00:17:11,457
It's true the three of us aren't related by blood.

313
00:17:11,797 --> 00:17:12,757
But we're family.

314
00:17:13,717 --> 00:17:16,117
All I've ever wanted was to be their mother.

315
00:17:17,217 --> 00:17:18,317
And now...

316
00:17:18,317 --> 00:17:19,397
Now I can be.

317
00:17:19,397 --> 00:17:30,957
I wish I could have been a better mother to the both of you girls.

318
00:17:31,017 --> 00:17:31,877
Don't say that!

319
00:17:31,897 --> 00:17:34,057
We don't need anything, just don't die!

320
00:17:34,237 --> 00:17:34,537
Nami.

321
00:17:35,817 --> 00:17:38,037
Go and make your dreams come true.

322
00:17:38,897 --> 00:17:39,857
For me.

323
00:17:41,157 --> 00:17:41,597
Hmph.

324
00:17:43,217 --> 00:17:43,817
So.

325
00:17:44,617 --> 00:17:46,617
You ready to die, human?

326
00:17:46,897 --> 00:17:47,437
Nochiko!

327
00:17:47,657 --> 00:17:47,977
Nami!

328
00:17:47,977 --> 00:17:57,277
Love you.

329
00:18:02,217 --> 00:18:04,577
I'm joining the Arlong Pirates.

330
00:18:05,537 --> 00:18:08,157
I'll get to be a navigator and draw maps.

331
00:18:08,397 --> 00:18:08,797
Nami.

332
00:18:09,637 --> 00:18:13,197
I made a deal with Arlong to buy Kokoyashi Village from it.

333
00:18:13,297 --> 00:18:14,437
Buy Kokoyashi?

334
00:18:14,857 --> 00:18:15,337
How?

335
00:18:15,557 --> 00:18:17,397
For a hundred million berries.

336
00:18:17,397 --> 00:18:19,297
But a hundred million berries?

337
00:18:19,577 --> 00:18:21,897
You can't earn that working your whole life!

338
00:18:21,957 --> 00:18:24,117
I will get that money no matter what!

339
00:18:26,137 --> 00:18:28,937
If anyone tries to help me, they'll just get hurt.

340
00:18:28,937 --> 00:18:44,297
Good things will come your way, as long as you continue to live.

341
00:18:44,717 --> 00:18:45,717
I'll be okay.

342
00:18:46,257 --> 00:18:49,337
I'll just smile every time I see his face.

343
00:18:49,337 --> 00:18:51,277
I'm not going to cry anymore.

344
00:18:51,277 --> 00:18:54,237
I'm going to fight by myself.

345
00:19:01,677 --> 00:19:03,577
I miss her so much.

346
00:19:03,577 --> 00:19:08,717
This waiting is killing me.

347
00:19:09,257 --> 00:19:11,917
I'll steal every memory they have left.

348
00:19:12,257 --> 00:19:13,877
Each and every one.

349
00:19:13,877 --> 00:19:21,217
Oh, man.

350
00:19:21,377 --> 00:19:22,017
I'm sorry.

351
00:19:22,097 --> 00:19:22,737
Did I wake you?

352
00:19:22,957 --> 00:19:23,357
No.

353
00:19:23,517 --> 00:19:25,037
Go on back to sleep if you want.

354
00:19:25,297 --> 00:19:27,497
I'll wake you up if I notice anything strange.

355
00:19:27,837 --> 00:19:28,537
I'm okay.

356
00:19:28,797 --> 00:19:30,057
But thanks for keeping a lookout.

357
00:19:30,437 --> 00:19:32,597
How about I brew some coffee to help keep us up?

358
00:19:32,897 --> 00:19:33,937
That sounds great.

359
00:19:34,057 --> 00:19:35,157
I could sure use some.

360
00:19:35,157 --> 00:19:37,717
Well, he didn't waste any damn time, did he?

361
00:19:37,977 --> 00:19:40,157
And right after he swore he wouldn't fall asleep.

362
00:19:45,377 --> 00:19:46,997
What are you two doing up?

363
00:19:47,117 --> 00:19:48,877
Everyone here is supposed to be asleep.

364
00:19:49,077 --> 00:19:51,437
So you're the thief who stole everyone's memories.

365
00:19:52,337 --> 00:19:54,157
I'm surprised you realized.

366
00:19:56,257 --> 00:19:58,137
Not that you can do anything about it.

367
00:20:02,897 --> 00:20:03,717
Come on.

368
00:20:03,877 --> 00:20:04,417
Wake up.

369
00:20:05,157 --> 00:20:07,157
Ah, you've got mystical abilities.

370
00:20:07,677 --> 00:20:08,037
Eh.

371
00:20:08,617 --> 00:20:09,057
What?

372
00:20:09,437 --> 00:20:09,837
Ah!

373
00:20:10,617 --> 00:20:11,397
He's back!

374
00:20:11,397 --> 00:20:11,657
Ah!

375
00:20:12,477 --> 00:20:14,397
Is it already breakfast time?

376
00:20:14,497 --> 00:20:15,797
That wasn't very nice.

377
00:20:15,997 --> 00:20:17,537
You should have just let them sleep.

378
00:20:17,757 --> 00:20:19,617
I really didn't want to have to do this.

379
00:20:19,837 --> 00:20:21,557
But you've given me no other choice.

380
00:20:31,397 --> 00:20:31,637
Ah!

381
00:20:32,577 --> 00:20:34,497
What do you think you're doing up there?

382
00:20:34,617 --> 00:20:34,857
Huh?

383
00:20:34,857 --> 00:20:36,537
Who said you could sit there?

384
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:37,697
It's mine!

385
00:20:37,817 --> 00:20:39,397
I cleaned it earlier today!

386
00:20:39,737 --> 00:20:42,737
Don't you dare sit there!

387
00:20:42,737 --> 00:20:43,297
Huh?

388
00:20:43,297 --> 00:20:57,337
Sorry I took your seat.

389
00:20:57,337 --> 00:21:02,757
What the heck is this stuff?

390
00:21:02,757 --> 00:21:03,377
What's happening to him?

391
00:21:03,377 --> 00:21:07,437
What's happening to him?

392
00:21:07,437 --> 00:21:08,437
I'm scared.

393
00:21:08,437 --> 00:21:08,557
I'm scared.

394
00:21:15,137 --> 00:21:15,437
What?

395
00:21:15,437 --> 00:21:16,717
What was that?

396
00:21:16,717 --> 00:21:18,977
Hey, shouldn't we do something for him?

397
00:21:18,977 --> 00:21:20,597
He's not moving.

398
00:21:20,597 --> 00:21:22,837
He's still alive, isn't he?

399
00:21:22,837 --> 00:21:22,857
He's still alive, isn't he?

400
00:21:22,857 --> 00:21:23,437
Doctor!

401
00:21:23,437 --> 00:21:23,937
Doctor!

402
00:21:23,937 --> 00:21:24,277
Doctor!

403
00:21:24,277 --> 00:21:25,977
All right, that's me.

404
00:21:26,477 --> 00:21:26,937
Huh?

405
00:21:26,937 --> 00:21:27,437
He...

406
00:21:27,437 --> 00:21:28,937
Huh?

407
00:21:28,937 --> 00:21:33,617
I got all my memories back!

408
00:21:33,617 --> 00:21:46,317
I can't.

409
00:21:46,457 --> 00:21:51,337
I can't.

410
00:21:51,337 --> 00:22:21,317
We'll see you next time.

411
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:07,691
On the next, Wood Piece.

412
00:23:07,911 --> 00:23:09,571
Now let's get back our memories.

413
00:23:09,991 --> 00:23:11,991
The pirate crew lands on the island.

414
00:23:12,271 --> 00:23:14,151
I'm gonna cut you jerks down.

